doc:sec-48 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "48 Simplified outline of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "This Part establishes the Creative Workplaces Council. The function of the Creative Workplaces Council is to advise the Board about the responsibilities of Creative Workplaces. The Board may also direct the Council to perform a particular function, or exercise a particular power, of Creative Australia. The Council consists of the Chair of the Council and 6 other members, all of whom are appointed by the Minister. The CEO is not eligible for appointment. This Part also deals with the terms and conditions of appointment for Council members and the procedures of the Council." ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

