concept:creative-australia-act-2023-sec-72 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "72 Termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-72 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Board may, with the written agreement of the Minister, terminate the appointment of the CEO: (a) for misbehaviour; or (b) if the CEO is unable to perform the duties of the CEO’s office because of physical or mental incapacity; or (c) if the Board is satisfied that the performance of the CEO has been unsatisfactory for a significant period; or (d) if the CEO: (i) becomes bankrupt; or" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Board may, with the written agreement of the Minister, terminate the appointment of the CEO: (a) for misbehaviour; or (b) if the CEO is unable to perform the duties of the CEO’s office because of physical or mental incapacity; or (c) if the Board is satisfied that the performance of the CEO has been unsatisfactory for a significant period; or (d) if the CEO: (i) becomes bankrupt; or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a975e1b71058e076661883a5c5d7d936bbc3df0bd8d30d969e5c7773990c12d8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Board may terminate the appointment of the CEO under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <creative-australia-act-2023.pdf> ;
    dc:source "creative-australia-act-2023.pdf, p.71" ;
    cml:asserts concept:creative-australia-act-2023-sec-72-norm .
